      "Trust is the invisible thread that holds a workplace together. In today's competitive business world, building mutual trust between employers and employees is not merely desirable but essential, for it shapes how effectively an organization performs and grows.",
      "On the one hand, trust boosts efficiency and reduces internal friction. When employers trust their staff with greater autonomy, employees feel respected and work with genuine initiative rather than fear. On the other hand, mutual trust strengthens loyalty and a sense of belonging. Take Google as an example: by granting engineers freedom to spend part of their time on personal projects, the company earned deep employee commitment, and this trust in turn gave birth to innovations such as Gmail. Clearly, when both sides believe in each other, cooperation replaces suspicion.",
